window.JOURNAL = [{"ord":228,"md":"Armasse. The host of **Deskari** came down on **Kenabres**, and the Worldwound came into the city with it. The first day of the whole affair."},{"ord":235,"md":"The **Gray Garrison** stormed and the ruined wardstone destroyed. Mythic power came to the company on that ground."},{"ord":237,"md":"The **Vineyard Hills Waystation** delivered out of a demon attack."},{"ord":242,"md":"**Rabiah's Redeemers** marched for **Drezen**."},{"ord":245,"md":"On the road. The quartermaster's count stood at forty-seven. *(GM's hand)*"},{"ord":246,"md":"Forty-seven units of food and supply on the rolls."},{"ord":247,"md":"The count fell to forty-four."},{"ord":248,"md":"Forty-four still. The column camped below the **Lost Chapel**, on the road to Drezen."},{"ord":249,"md":"Camped within sight of **Drezen**. The horses were poisoned in the night. *(GM's hand)*"},{"ord":250,"md":"The **Battle of Paradise Hill**; the **Battle of Southbank**; and Paradise Hill fought a second time when the ghouls came. *(GM's hand)*"},{"ord":251,"md":"The courtyard of Drezen taken."},{"ord":252,"md":"The clearing of **Citadel Drezen** begun — the sally port, the **Templar's Court**, the **West Garrison**, the **Inheritor's Temple**."},{"ord":253,"md":"The **berbalang** dealt with, and the first word of **Callan Thornwind**."},{"ord":254,"md":"Back into the citadel: the third day of the assault on the first floor."},{"ord":255,"md":"**Staunton Vhane** buried. ***Soul Shear*** unmade in the forge, and the dungeons beneath Drezen entered."},{"ord":256,"md":"Drezen taken, and the ***Sword of Valor*** recovered."},{"ord":257,"md":"**Sir Aldrich Thorne** came from the Queen as steward, and Drezen passed to **Irabeth Tirabade** to rule."},{"ord":264,"md":"The first week of Drezen's recovery."},{"ord":271,"md":"The second week."},{"ord":278,"md":"The third week of recovery in Drezen."},{"ord":285,"md":"Out from Drezen, to look into a cultist site rumoured in the **Marchlands**."},{"ord":286,"md":"The second day toward the **Fallen Fane**, along the **Ahari** riverbed. A hail of teeth drove the company under a bridge; when the weather broke they looked briefly at the abandoned town by the water and pressed on."},{"ord":287,"md":"The third day. They reached the head of the Ahari, and came out of the riverbed into swarming ticks. They fell back and struck south."},{"ord":288,"md":"The fourth day, after a cold night nobody had dressed for — the Worldwound taking its toll on the unprepared. **Cornelia** took a vulture's shape to scout. A patrol was sighted and its backtrail followed to the cliffs, and the company slept in a cave."},{"ord":289,"md":"An old, well-worn trail down the cliffs, and a wide cave holding a temple of **Baphomet** kept as a cultists' waystation. **Varic** knew it for a defiled house of **Sarenrae**, and it drove him into a rage."},{"ord":290,"md":"The night spent inside the **Fallen Fane**."},{"ord":291,"md":"Homeward for Drezen. Ashstorms slowed them."},{"ord":292,"md":"Still on the road, camped at a shack near the Ahari riverbed."},{"ord":293,"md":"Drezen again, and news waiting: a priest missing, and caravans being taken."},{"ord":294,"md":"The disappearance of **Jeskar Hinton** looked into."},{"ord":295,"md":"Out for the **Weeping Hills**."},{"ord":296,"md":"The **Weeping Hills** reached."},{"ord":297,"md":"Turned back toward Drezen."},{"ord":298,"md":"Still bound for Drezen, the Weeping Hills' treasure carried out with them."},{"ord":299,"md":"Met with **Irabeth**, and commissioned scrolls of ***Secure Shelter***."},{"ord":300,"md":"The trek toward the temple of **Sarenrae** begun. The hunting came to nothing."},{"ord":301,"md":"They woke to a rain of acidic ooze."},{"ord":302,"md":"Camp broken, and a new day's march."},{"ord":303,"md":"Dead cultists on the ground, and a mount carrying a message that named **Jaruunicka** and **Takira's Redoubt**."},{"ord":304,"md":"The cliffs before the **Gray Road**. Bodaks found them while they gathered firewood."},{"ord":305,"md":"They came again to the Fallen Fane, no longer fallen. A storm of lightning and bursting air met them there."},{"ord":306,"md":"The day spent digging out the temple of **Sarenrae**."},{"ord":307,"md":"The ground around the new temple explored."},{"ord":308,"md":"A dream at dawn sent **Harlock** and the company chasing south."},{"ord":309,"md":"An abyssal rift-storm washed **Lupenor** and **Chyrrik** downstream."},{"ord":310,"md":"Toward the place of Harlock's dream, and the long way about. **Rabiah** felt herself watched."},{"ord":311,"md":"Across the **Gray Road** and along the shore of the lava lake. **Abner Suthi** died in the **Molten Scar**, and the mythic vrock **Vorimeraak** was slain there."},{"ord":312,"md":"Back by teleport to the temple of Sarenrae. Rabiah studied the ground; the night passed indoors."},{"ord":313,"md":"Out from the temple of **Sarenrae**, north along the rim of the great inland sea by an unfamiliar route, followers in train and the hunters of **Erastil** among them."},{"ord":314,"md":"Second day out. **Selyse Avelia**'s bird taken; the **babau**'s parley on the road; the Derakni ambush. **Selyse** read a scroll and was gone. A forced march was argued for and voted down; the company made a fortified camp ten miles from **Drezen** instead, **Varic** walling the horses in and sitting the night out beside them."},{"ord":315,"md":"Into **Drezen** before noon. The spoils sold, the great uncut diamond traded away, **Abner Suthi** raised in the temple of **Sarenrae** at **Varic**'s own expense. The mural on **Rabiah**'s wall. **Horgus Gwerm** asked for paladins and got them."},{"ord":316,"md":"Breakfast with **Abner**; the charm bracelet given and unmasked as a beacon. **Gretcher** marched them to the Citadel, where **Anevia** asked them to plant the Queen's spy at the shrine and **Takira's Redoubt** surfaced on **Selyse**'s new map. **Smendrick** the jeweller; the watcher turned back down his own thread; **Horgus**'s escort recalled and refused. That evening **Chyrrik** and three paladins went out to the shrine and **Elara Dawnstrider** came home, by way of two badly missed teleports."},{"ord":317,"md":"The Queen's agent collected from the temple pews, and the company carried west to the **Hidden Shrine**, where they spent the night and turned their minds to the dragon."},{"ord":318,"md":"Out of the **Hidden Shrine** into an ash storm blowing up off the lava country, south along the rim of the **Gray Road**. Half a hex of ground all day, and camp in a crevice of the old riverbed."},{"ord":319,"md":"The great clawed footprint, the shattered obsidian knight of **Iomedae** in the riverbed, and the cave in the western bank. They went in the same evening rather than sleep beside it, and killed the woundwyrm **Scorizscar** in her own lair."},{"ord":320,"md":"From the dragon's lair by teleport to the temple of Sarenrae, where they sat out the storm."},{"ord":321,"md":"Out from the temple toward the redoubt."},{"ord":322,"md":"On the Gray Road, west for **Takira's Redoubt**. **Lupenor** woke from a dream of the place. The **Red Swarm** took them on the road."},{"ord":323,"md":"Marching for the redoubt."},{"ord":324,"md":"**Takira's Redoubt** reached."},{"ord":325,"md":"Teleport to the Hidden Shrine: goods set down, orders left, **Chyrrik** posted as runner, **Samail** raised — and back to the redoubt, mostly by teleport again."},{"ord":326,"md":"A storm of teeth held them from leaving for the **Green Gates** and the **Ivory Sanctum**. Rabiah's needle and thread built the first bridge to her new succubus companion."},{"ord":327,"md":"Toward the Green Gates, with **Arueshalae** guiding."},{"ord":328,"md":"The same road, the same guide."},{"ord":329,"md":"The climb to the **Green Gates**."},{"ord":330,"md":"The **Ivory Sanctum** assaulted."}];
window.MAPS = [{"id":"marchlands","order":1,"title":"The Marchlands","subtitle":"The broken country west of Drezen — badlands, canyon and lava, and the road the crusade came in by","image":"images/map-marchlands.webp","scale":"one hex — twelve miles, or a hard day's march","surface":[[13.6,8.5],[83.2,5.0],[87.8,82.5],[8.6,77.4]],"hexes":[9.7,5.67],"intro":"The Marchlands are what Sarkoria became. Dry ridges and dust where there were fields, a river run\nout of its bed, and the whole southern horizon lit orange after dark. The crusade came in along\nthe eastern rivers and fought for every crossing; everything west of the lava the company walked\nfor itself. **Selyse Avelia** was hired to put it all down on one chart, and the places on it are\nthe places they earned.","places":[{"id":"drezen","name":"Drezen","x":67.0,"y":21.0,"kind":"city","style":"pin","letter":"A","revealed":true,"chapter":"The Liberation of Drezen City","chapterId":"ch20","chapterLabel":"Book II — Chapter VIII","md":"The liberated citadel, and the only walls in three days' march. Every expedition into the\nMarchlands begins at its western gate and is counted home through the same arch — battered,\nacid-scarred, and short of somebody.","text":"Drezen The liberated citadel, and the only walls in three days' march. Every expedition into the Marchlands begins at its western gate and is counted home through the same arch — battered, acid-scarred, and short of somebody."},{"id":"the-abandoned-swarm-caverns","name":"The Abandoned Swarm Caverns","x":73.0,"y":22.8,"kind":"lair","style":"pin","letter":"B","revealed":true,"chapter":"The Nest","chapterId":"ch19","chapterLabel":"Book II — Chapter VII","md":"Under the canyon floor, where boiling green vapour hung over the ground and the eye could pick\nout the swarms drifting in it — ***vescavors***, abyssal colony-things that devour metal and skin\nalike, ruled by a queen. The company went down and burned her. The caverns have been quiet since.","text":"The Abandoned Swarm Caverns Under the canyon floor, where boiling green vapour hung over the ground and the eye could pick out the swarms drifting in it — vescavors , abyssal colony-things that devour metal and skin alike, ruled by a queen. The company went down and burned her. The caverns have been quiet since."},{"id":"the-lost-chapel","name":"The Lost Chapel","x":78.5,"y":22.0,"kind":"temple","style":"pin","letter":"C","revealed":true,"chapter":"The Lost Chapel","chapterId":"ch18","chapterLabel":"Book II — Chapter VI","md":"A ghoul-den one morning and a chapel again by the next. The dead were carried out and the filth\nwith them, and the altar of the **Inheritor** stood clean. When the company climbed back out of\nthe nest below, the chapel above them was still standing quiet — a light in the canyon where\nthere had not been one.","text":"The Lost Chapel A ghoul-den one morning and a chapel again by the next. The dead were carried out and the filth with them, and the altar of the Inheritor stood clean. When the company climbed back out of the nest below, the chapel above them was still standing quiet — a light in the canyon where there had not been one."},{"id":"keeper-s-canyon","name":"Keeper's Canyon","x":82.5,"y":28.5,"kind":"peril","style":"pin","letter":"D","revealed":true,"chapter":"The Battle of Keeper's Canyon","chapterId":"ch17","chapterLabel":"Book II — Chapter V","md":"Where the road west turns toward **Drezen**, and where **Lupenor** and **Anevia** came up onto\nhigh ground at dusk and looked down on two armies camped in it. The crusade did not walk into\nthat canyon in the dark. **Exorius** held it that morning; by evening he held nothing, and came\nthrough a sleeping camp that night for the girl who commanded it.","text":"Keeper's Canyon Where the road west turns toward Drezen , and where Lupenor and Anevia came up onto high ground at dusk and looked down on two armies camped in it. The crusade did not walk into that canyon in the dark. Exorius held it that morning; by evening he held nothing, and came through a sleeping camp that night for the girl who commanded it."},{"id":"vilareth-ford","name":"Vilareth Ford","x":76.4,"y":57.5,"kind":"water","style":"pin","letter":"E","revealed":true,"chapter":"The Battle of Vilareth Ford","chapterId":"ch16","chapterLabel":"Book II — Chapter IV","md":"The crossing on the road up from **Kenabres**. It had already fallen when the scouts brought word\nback to the column — which is the only reason it was won. **Kamilo Dann** held a dozen wounded\ncrusaders together in a stone gaol until the Redeemers took the ford back, then carried word of\nits fall south down the road.","text":"Vilareth Ford The crossing on the road up from Kenabres . It had already fallen when the scouts brought word back to the column — which is the only reason it was won. Kamilo Dann held a dozen wounded crusaders together in a stone gaol until the Redeemers took the ford back, then carried word of its fall south down the road."},{"id":"delamere-s-tomb","name":"Delamere's Tomb","x":61.0,"y":48.5,"kind":"ruin","style":"pin","letter":"G","revealed":true,"chapter":"The Stag King's Bride","chapterId":"ch35","chapterLabel":"Book III — Chapter IV","md":"In a cave off the lava tunnel, down in the **Weeping Hills** — a two-hundred-foot gorge with a\nriver of lava at the bottom and walls that weep, molten stone dripping from the rock face in\nteardrops that sizzle and pool and rejoin the flow. **Delamere** lies interred here, and a demon\nwearing **Jeskar Hinton** stood over the drop with no intention of coming back up.","text":"Delamere's Tomb In a cave off the lava tunnel, down in the Weeping Hills — a two-hundred-foot gorge with a river of lava at the bottom and walls that weep, molten stone dripping from the rock face in teardrops that sizzle and pool and rejoin the flow. Delamere lies interred here, and a demon wearing Jeskar Hinton stood over the drop with no intention of coming back up."},{"id":"the-molten-cascade","name":"The Molten Cascade","x":50.5,"y":51.0,"kind":"peril","style":"pin","letter":"I","revealed":true,"chapter":"","chapterId":"","chapterLabel":"","md":"Where the dry river, the lava and the canyon country all arrive at once, and the fire comes down\nin steps. Nothing crosses here that does not mean to.","text":"The Molten Cascade Where the dry river, the lava and the canyon country all arrive at once, and the fire comes down in steps. Nothing crosses here that does not mean to."},{"id":"the-family-crypt","name":"The Family Crypt","x":60.5,"y":16.5,"kind":"ruin","style":"pin","letter":"J","revealed":true,"chapter":"The Homeward Trail","chapterId":"ch34","chapterLabel":"Book III — Chapter III","md":"A Sarkorian burial ground north of the road home. **Varic** walked too close to it and felt\nsomething lurch in his chest — a cold coming off one crypt in particular that made the hair stand\nup on his arms. *We'll clear it. You have my word.* The word is still outstanding.","text":"The Family Crypt A Sarkorian burial ground north of the road home. Varic walked too close to it and felt something lurch in his chest — a cold coming off one crypt in particular that made the hair stand up on his arms. We'll clear it. You have my word. The word is still outstanding."},{"id":"the-sarian-fane","name":"The Sarian Fane","x":50.0,"y":31.0,"kind":"temple","style":"pin","letter":"K","revealed":true,"chapter":"The Fane Remade","chapterId":"ch33","chapterLabel":"Book III — Chapter II","md":"A shrine of **Sarenrae** at the foot of a cliff path, taken by the Templars of the Ivory\nLabyrinth and kept as a waystation — beds in a row and not one personal effect in the place,\nwhich told the company how many of the Labyrinth were moving through this country. **Zinedra**\nheld it. She does not hold it now. It stands sanctified for the first time in longer than anyone\ncan guess, and carries a priest of the Dawnflower's name.","text":"The Sarian Fane A shrine of Sarenrae at the foot of a cliff path, taken by the Templars of the Ivory Labyrinth and kept as a waystation — beds in a row and not one personal effect in the place, which told the company how many of the Labyrinth were moving through this country. Zinedra held it. She does not hold it now. It stands sanctified for the first time in longer than anyone can guess, and carries a priest of the Dawnflower's name."},{"id":"scorizscar-s-lair","name":"Scorizscar's Lair","x":47.5,"y":44.5,"kind":"lair","style":"pin","letter":"L","revealed":true,"chapter":"The Beacon and the Wyrm","chapterId":"ch40","chapterLabel":"Book III — Chapter IX","md":"A cave mouth in the western bank of the dry riverbed, past a field of broken wagons. Obsidian\nflakes glittering underfoot, long parallel gouges along a thirty-foot ceiling, and three obsidian\nhooves snapped off where the rest of the horse had shattered. **Scorizscar** came down out of the\ndark — six-legged, eyeless, and the wrong number of teeth besides — and did not go back up.","text":"Scorizscar's Lair A cave mouth in the western bank of the dry riverbed, past a field of broken wagons. Obsidian flakes glittering underfoot, long parallel gouges along a thirty-foot ceiling, and three obsidian hooves snapped off where the rest of the horse had shattered. Scorizscar came down out of the dark — six-legged, eyeless, and the wrong number of teeth besides — and did not go back up."},{"id":"the-molten-scar","name":"The Molten Scar","x":52.0,"y":61.0,"kind":"peril","style":"pin","letter":"M","revealed":true,"chapter":"Fury Repaid","chapterId":"ch38","chapterLabel":"Book III — Chapter VII","md":"A chamber open to a sky that flickered red, rimmed by rock walls, with the lava working below it.\n**Vorimeraak** led the ritual here, scythe in hand and a merchant chained to a spike on the stone —\nand it was the same ritual that had been worked on **Harlock** at fifteen, three hundred yards from\nwhere he now stood. He killed her, and the whole of that night came back in the instant she died.","text":"The Molten Scar A chamber open to a sky that flickered red, rimmed by rock walls, with the lava working below it. Vorimeraak led the ritual here, scythe in hand and a merchant chained to a spike on the stone — and it was the same ritual that had been worked on Harlock at fifteen, three hundred yards from where he now stood. He killed her, and the whole of that night came back in the instant she died."},{"id":"arueshalae-s-redoubt","name":"Arueshalae's Redoubt","x":20.0,"y":20.0,"kind":"city","style":"pin","letter":"N","revealed":true,"chapter":"The Gates of the Redoubt","chapterId":"ch43","chapterLabel":"Book III — Chapter XII","md":"**Takira's Redoubt**, on the charts and in the cultists' own dispatches — a fort that rises out\nof the frozen Marchlands in the far west, among the last of the standing woods. **Lupenor** knew\nit before she saw it, stone for stone, out of a dream. The demonic host had hunted **Arueshalae**\nthe length of the Worldwound and posted a thousand platinum for her, and a captured order named\nthe place outright: *Jaruunicka has tracked her to Takira's Redoubt. Send reinforcements\nimmediately.* The courier never delivered it and the reinforcements never came. The company got\nthere first — and what met them at the gates wore her face.","text":"Arueshalae's Redoubt Takira's Redoubt , on the charts and in the cultists' own dispatches — a fort that rises out of the frozen Marchlands in the far west, among the last of the standing woods. Lupenor knew it before she saw it, stone for stone, out of a dream. The demonic host had hunted Arueshalae the length of the Worldwound and posted a thousand platinum for her, and a captured order named the place outright: Jaruunicka has tracked her to Takira's Redoubt. Send reinforcements immediately. The courier never delivered it and the reinforcements never came. The company got there first — and what met them at the gates wore her face."},{"id":"the-ivory-sanctum","name":"The Ivory Sanctum","x":37.5,"y":52.0,"kind":"lair","style":"pin","letter":"O","revealed":true,"chapter":"The Jailer's Ring","chapterId":"ch46","chapterLabel":"Book III — Chapter XV","md":"Behind the Greengates — a wall of grey stone mottled with lichen, woody vines curled across it,\nthe thorns barbed and even the insects on it correct. It is a masterwork of a lie, and the door\nis real. Beyond it: the elixirs, and the worm that walks whom **Staunton Vhane**'s own journals\nnamed with dread.","text":"The Ivory Sanctum Behind the Greengates — a wall of grey stone mottled with lichen, woody vines curled across it, the thorns barbed and even the insects on it correct. It is a masterwork of a lie, and the door is real. Beyond it: the elixirs, and the worm that walks whom Staunton Vhane 's own journals named with dread."},{"id":"kenabres","name":"Kenabres","x":75.5,"y":67.5,"kind":"city","style":"pin","letter":"","revealed":true,"chapter":"The Gathering in the Dark","chapterId":"ch1","chapterLabel":"Book I — Chapter I","md":"Downriver on the eastern bank, and the reason there is a crusade at all. The city fell in an\nafternoon; everything the company has done since began in the dark under it.","text":"Kenabres Downriver on the eastern bank, and the reason there is a crusade at all. The city fell in an afternoon; everything the company has done since began in the dark under it."},{"id":"the-waystation-at-vineyard-hills","name":"The Waystation at Vineyard Hills","x":83.5,"y":68.0,"kind":"camp","style":"pin","letter":"","revealed":true,"chapter":"The Waystation at Vineyard Hills","chapterId":"ch13","chapterLabel":"Book II — Chapter I","md":"A stop on the road east of **Kenabres**, and the last ordinary place any of them stood before the\nmarch north.","text":"The Waystation at Vineyard Hills A stop on the road east of Kenabres , and the last ordinary place any of them stood before the march north."}]}];